Subject: [PATCH] usb: lge_ds3: retry ds_dp_config() on -ENODEV instead of tearing down USB host

When the Dual Screen is already attached at power-on, lge_ds3 reaches DS_Startup
before dp_display_probe() has registered the DisplayPort USBPD SVID handler --
a miss of only a few milliseconds. usbpd_find_dp_handler() returns NULL and
ds_dp_config() fails with -ENODEV, which is a timing miss rather than a real
failure.

The existing error path treats it as fatal and calls stop_2nd_usb_host(), which
lands roughly 82us after start_2nd_usb_host(). dwc3 consequently sees host:1
immediately followed by host:0, brings the xHCI host up and then tears it back
down while the hub is still enumerating the DS2:

  [1.041164] start_2nd_usb_host: EXTCON_USB_HOST=0 -> 1
  [1.041240] ds_dp_config: No DP handler found
  [1.041246] stop_2nd_usb_host: EXTCON_USB_HOST=1 -> 0
  [1.041361] dwc3_otg_start_host: turn on host
  [1.045274] dp_display_probe          <-- handler registers, ~4ms too late
  [1.096377] xhci-hcd.1.auto: new USB bus registered, assigned bus number 1
  [1.099259] dwc3_otg_start_host: turn off host

That teardown deadlocks. hub_quiesce() blocks forever in flush_delayed_work(),
so dwc3_otg_sm_work never returns; dwc3_resume_work then blocks in
flush_delayed_work(&mdwc->sm_work), the first statement of
dwc3_ext_event_notify(). Since dwc3_wq is alloc_ordered_workqueue(..., 0) with
max_active 1, every subsequent queue_work() piles up behind the blocked item and
never runs, leaving dwc3 permanently deaf to USB ID changes. Confirmed with
sysrq-w:

  kworker/u16:10 +k_sm_usb   D        kworker/u16:11 +dwc3_wq   D
    dwc3_otg_sm_work                    dwc3_resume_work
    dwc3_otg_start_host                 dwc3_ext_event_notify
    xhci_plat_remove                    flush_delayed_work
    usb_remove_hcd                      __flush_work
    usb_disconnect                      wait_for_completion
    hub_disconnect
    hub_quiesce
    wait_for_completion

The user-visible symptom is repeated "hub failed to enable device, error -108",
lge_ds3 looping DS_USB_Wait -> DS_Recovery_* forever, and only a reboot clearing
it. UsbService and the dualscreen HAL also end up blocked behind it.

Retry ds_dp_config() across the registration window rather than tearing the host
back down. Any error other than -ENODEV, and -ENODEV past the retry budget,
still takes the original path.

Note the retry must also bypass the is_ds_connected guard at the top of
STATE_DS_STARTUP. That flag is set before ds_dp_config() is called, so a plain
re-entry returns early and never reaches the retried call: USB then enumerates
cleanly while is_dp_configured stays false and the DP link never comes up
("ds2_pd_store: dp is not configured"). The goto deliberately skips the connect
work above it, which has already run once and would otherwise enable regulators
a second time.

Tested on an LG V60 ThinQ (timelm) running LineageOS, booting with the Dual
Screen attached from power-on:

  [1.037221] ds_dp_config: No DP handler found
  [1.037229] DP handler not ready, retry 1/40 in 50ms
  [1.087277] ds_dp_config: config:1
  [30.619265] EDID read successed, count=1
  [30.628391] link training #1 successful
  [30.630483] link training #2 successful

Zero "error -108", DS_Ready reached with no DS_Recovery_* cycling, no blocked
k_sm_usb/dwc3_wq workers, and Android enumerates the second panel as a
1080x2460 external display.

--- a/drivers/usb/misc/lge_ds3.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/misc/lge_ds3.c
@@ -263,6 +263,7 @@
 	bool				acc_det_vadc;
 	int				acc_det_count;
 	int				pd_active;
+	int				dp_cfg_retry;
 
 	u8				tx_msgid;
 	enum pd_spec_rev		spec_rev;
@@ -490,6 +491,16 @@
 			attention[hpd].len - 1);
 }
 
+/*
+ * ds_dp_config() returns -ENODEV until the DisplayPort USBPD SVID handler has
+ * registered. With the Dual Screen already attached at power-on this state
+ * machine reaches DS_Startup at ~1.037s while dp_display_probe() only lands a
+ * few milliseconds later. Retry across that window instead of treating it as a
+ * hard failure.
+ */
+#define DS_DP_CONFIG_RETRY_MS	50
+#define DS_DP_CONFIG_MAX_RETRY	40	/* 2s total; the race is only a few ms wide */
+
 static int ds_dp_config(struct ds3 *ds3, bool config)
 {
 	struct device *dev = ds3->dev;
@@ -1198,6 +1209,20 @@
 	case STATE_UNKNOWN:
 	case STATE_DS_STARTUP:
 		if (ds3->is_ds_connected) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_LGE_USB_DS_DIRECT_SVID
+			/*
+			 * A ds_dp_config() retry re-enters here with is_ds_connected
+			 * already set. Jump straight back to the DP configuration step:
+			 * the connect work below has run once already, and repeating it
+			 * would enable regulators a second time and re-drive the GPIOs.
+			 * Without this the retry returns here silently, ds_dp_config()
+			 * is never reached again, is_dp_configured stays false, and the
+			 * DP link never comes up ("ds2_pd_store: dp is not configured")
+			 * even though USB enumerates cleanly.
+			 */
+			if (ds3->dp_cfg_retry)
+				goto ds_dp_config_retry;
+#endif
 			dev_dbg(dev, "%s: DS2 is already connected\n",
 				__func__);
 			goto sm_done;
@@ -1231,17 +1256,45 @@
 						  &val);
 		}
 #else
+ds_dp_config_retry:
 		ret = ds_dp_config(ds3, true);
 		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * -ENODEV only means the DP SVID handler is not up yet -- a
+			 * timing miss, not a real failure. Do NOT fall into the
+			 * teardown below for it.
+			 *
+			 * start_2nd_usb_host() ran a few tens of microseconds ago, so
+			 * calling stop_2nd_usb_host() here makes dwc3 see host:1
+			 * immediately followed by host:0 and begin an xHCI teardown
+			 * while the hub is still enumerating the DS2. hub_quiesce()
+			 * then blocks forever, wedging dwc3_otg_sm_work and -- through
+			 * flush_delayed_work() in dwc3_ext_event_notify() -- the
+			 * ordered dwc3_wq queued behind it. dwc3 goes permanently deaf
+			 * to ID changes and every later attach fails to enumerate with
+			 * -108 until the phone is rebooted.
+			 */
+			if (ret == -ENODEV &&
+			    ds3->dp_cfg_retry < DS_DP_CONFIG_MAX_RETRY) {
+				ds3->dp_cfg_retry++;
+				dev_info(dev, "%s: DP handler not ready, retry %d/%d in %dms\n",
+					 __func__, ds3->dp_cfg_retry,
+					 DS_DP_CONFIG_MAX_RETRY,
+					 DS_DP_CONFIG_RETRY_MS);
+				kick_sm(ds3, DS_DP_CONFIG_RETRY_MS);
+				goto sm_done;
+			}
 #ifdef USE_2ND_USB
 			// Secondary USB
 			stop_2nd_usb_host(ds3);
 			gpiod_direction_output(ds3->dd_sw_sel, 0);
 #endif
 			ds3->is_ds_connected = false;
+			ds3->dp_cfg_retry = 0;
 			ds_set_state(ds3, STATE_UNKNOWN);
 			goto sm_done;
 		}
+		ds3->dp_cfg_retry = 0;
 #endif
 
 		ds3->spec_rev = USBPD_REV_30;
